## Review severities (shared with reviewers)

`review-ui-ux` rates these by this table. Change a row here, never in a reviewer. A row counts
only when the change touches the surface, and only on the surfaces **Applies to** names. A tier
is visibility; the severity is this table's. Overflow and reflow at a width are rated by
`layout-rendering.mdc`.

| Signal | A finding when | Default | Not a finding |
|---|---|---|---|
| Invented proof shipped as fact: stats, logos, testimonials, customers (Copy T1, principle 5) | it renders in shipped copy | `major` | content marked as sample; Storybook fixtures |
| Primary task unreachable by keyboard, or focus invisible on the primary flow (`outline: none` with no `:focus-visible`, `div onClick`) | Tab through the flow cannot finish the task or cannot see where focus is | `major`; `minor` on a non-primary control | a `:focus-visible` replacement exists |
| Text contrast below 4.5:1 (3:1 large) on primary content | the pair is on shipped primary text, measured or computed from the token pair | `major` | decorative text; a pair not measured (`info`) |
| Missing loading, empty or error state on a primary view; destructive action with no confirm or Undo | the view or action is primary | `major`; `minor` on a secondary view | a state the component library renders by default |
| Other WCAG floor misses: target under 24px, color-only status, no reduced-motion branch, placeholder-as-label, paste blocked, zoom disabled, missing accessible name | always | `minor`; `major` when it blocks the primary flow | an N/A the author recorded |
| T1 tell, or slop score ≥9 | counted per tier on the changed surface | `minor` | a tell `DESIGN.md`, the brief or the job context chose; invented proof, focus and missing states, which the rows above rate (they still count in the score) |
| T2 tell, hierarchy competition, inconsistent tokens, drift from `DESIGN.md` | always | `minor` | the same exemptions |
| T3 tell (generic CTA labels included), polish, or a visual claim with no measurement | always | `info` | — |
